You are a senior product designer building a mobile-first web app called CompCal. CompCal is a productivity accountability app where users check into calendar events, get verified by AI-powered webcam snapshots that they're focused on their task, and see their progress visualized as climbing a mountain. Friends see each other's climbers hiking up their own peaks in real time. The highest climber each day wins.

AESTHETIC REFERENCE: Studio Ghibli meets Apple Fitness. Warm, painterly, confident. Not corporate fintech. Not gamer-aggressive. Calm ambient energy with moments of delight when a climber advances. Think Alto's Odyssey, Monument Valley, and Linear had a baby.

DESIGN SYSTEM (LOCKED):

Palette — "Alpine Dawn":
- Background sky (top): soft peach #F4D8BA
- Background sky (bottom): warm cream #FBF2E4
- Mountain fill: deep sage #4A6B54
- Snow caps: off-white #FDFBF7
- Primary accent: terracotta #C66B52 (user's own climber, active states)
- Secondary: dusty rose #D99A8F (friends' climbers)
- Text primary: deep ink #1F2028
- Text secondary: warm gray #746B62
- Success green (verified focus): moss #6B8E5A
- Distraction flag: soft coral #E89A7F (never red)

Typography:
- Headings and time displays: Instrument Serif
- Body: Inter
- Numbers, timers, scores: JetBrains Mono
- Type scale (use ONLY): 56px hero serif / 32px h1 serif / 20px h2 sans semibold / 16px body / 13px caption / 14px mono / 28px mono timer

Spacing: 4-point system. Allowed: 4, 8, 12, 16, 24, 32, 48, 64, 96.

Radius: 16px for cards, 999px for circular buttons/avatars, 8px for small inputs. Nothing else.

Shadow: ONE style for cards. 0 2px 8px rgba(31, 32, 40, 0.06), 0 12px 32px rgba(31, 32, 40, 0.04).

Viewport: Mobile-first, 430px max width. Center on desktop.

SCREENS TO PRODUCE (five total):

1. Home / Today screen:
   - Top section: today's date in serif, small subtitle "ready to climb?"
   - Today's calendar events as cards, each with event name, time, and a "Check In" primary button
   - Empty state card if no events: "add an event to your calendar to start climbing"
   - Bottom tab bar: Today (active), Mountain, Friends

2. Active check-in / Mountain screen (HERO SCREEN):
   - Full-bleed mountain illustration as background, SVG-generated in sage on cream gradient sky
   - User's climber avatar (terracotta circle with initial or photo) positioned on the mountain path at current progress height
   - Mountain has visible trail markers at 25%, 50%, 75%, 100% (summit)
   - Top HUD: task name in serif 20px, time remaining or elapsed in mono 28px
   - Floating bottom card: webcam thumbnail preview (small, 80x60px) + focus score as mono number (e.g., "97% focused") + last check indicator (moss dot = verified, coral dot = distracted)
   - Every 5-10 min when a snap happens, show a subtle toast at top: "Focus check ✓" or "Focus check ✗ — put the phone down" in caption text
   - When climber advances, small animation: climber moves up trail with 600ms ease-out
   - Top-right: pause button (ghost style)

3. Summit / Task complete screen:
   - Full screen takeover, mountain illustration with climber at peak, sun rising behind
   - Hero text in serif 56px: "summited" in terracotta
   - Below: task name, total focused time in mono 28px, focus score percentage
   - Share button (secondary): "share to friends' mountains"
   - Primary button: "back to today"

4. Friends / Leaderboard screen:
   - Three small mountains side by side at top, each with a tiny climber at their respective heights (this is the "at-a-glance" view of who's where right now)
   - Below: scrollable list of friends
   - Each row: avatar (circle, dusty rose border if currently climbing), name, current task (italic caption), focused time today in mono, altitude as percentage
   - Active climbers at top, completed climbers below, idle friends last
   - Time toggle pills: Today / This Week / This Month
   - User's own row highlighted with cream background and terracotta left border

5. Roast / Distraction intervention screen (the demo moment):
   - Appears as a modal overlay when user is flagged distracted 3+ times
   - Dark warm background #2B2028 with grain texture
   - Hero text in serif 32px: "caught slacking"
   - Below: AI-generated roast in serif 20px italic, centered, max 2 lines (e.g., "put the phone down, soldier. your ancestors didn't survive wars for you to scroll tiktok.")
   - Small caption: "shared with [friend names]" in mono
   - Primary button: "lock back in"
   - Ghost button: "take a break"
   - Subtle audio wave icon at top-right if ElevenLabs TTS is playing the roast

COMPONENTS TO DESIGN:

Mountain SVG: one master SVG file with:
- Layered path (foreground ridge, midground mountain, background peaks)
- Sage and cream palette
- Trail visible as dashed line going up
- Progress-based positions defined as percentage points along the trail
- Must animate smoothly between positions

Climber avatar: 
- Circular 32px default, 48px on own mountain, 24px on friends' mountains
- Border in accent color (terracotta for user, rose for friends)
- Tiny trail of footprints behind climber showing last 15% of progress

Focus check toast:
- Slides in from top, auto-dismisses after 2.5s
- Moss color for verified, coral for distracted
- Small icon (checkmark or X) in mono

Webcam preview:
- 80x60px floating card, 12px radius, subtle shadow
- Live video feed when active, frozen frame when snap is being processed
- Small pulsing dot when camera is active

ANIMATION RULES:
- Climber advance: 600ms ease-out, moves along SVG path
- Screen transitions: 300ms ease-out fade + 12px Y slide
- Toast: 200ms slide in, 300ms slide out
- Summit celebration: staggered reveal, mountain → climber → text → score, 1.5s total
- Roast appearance: background fade (400ms), text typewriter (40ms per char), audio starts after text completes
- Never use bouncing, spring, or overshoot animations

ABSOLUTELY FORBIDDEN:
- No purple anywhere
- No sparkle emojis, no decorative emojis
- No gamer-aggressive UI (no neon, no dark mode default, no "LEVEL UP!!" popups)
- No shame language in roasts beyond behavior (never attack identity or appearance)
- No red for distractions (use soft coral)
- No circular progress rings (too Apple Fitness)
- No pie charts or bar charts for focus data
- No stock illustration avatars
- No "streak flame" emoji or icons
- No gradients on buttons
- No hover bounce, no card lift, no rotation
- No "Welcome back!" greetings

COPY RULES:
- All roasts: direct, military drill-sergeant style, focus on behavior only, under 20 words
- Progress language is always positive: "climbing", "advancing", "summited", never "failed" or "behind"
- Friends screen uses geographic language: "altitude", "on the trail", "at base camp"
- Focus scores are shown as percentages, never as letter grades

OUTPUT:
Generate all five screens in mobile-first fidelity. Include at least three states for the mountain screen (early climb at 20%, mid-climb at 55%, summit at 100%). Show a friends screen populated with 5 realistic climber states (3 actively climbing at different heights, 1 summited, 1 idle). Show the roast modal with a real example roast.